        "title": "Simplify existing PR input initialization",
        "body": "Use the simplest input-freezing behavior needed for a Run.\n\nConceptually:\n\n```text\nresolve existing PR\n  \u2193\nfetch the concrete head/base commits needed for the Run\n  \u2193\nretain those exact commits as the Run input\n  \u2193\nstart execution\n```\n\nDo not add repeated API/fetch/API reconciliation solely to detect a hypothetical metadata race during initialization.\n\nOnce concrete commits have been fetched and retained, the Run should use those frozen commits as its input state.\n\nIf a later action needs to operate on the current Pull Request, that action can evaluate the current state at execution time.\n\nThis change implements the behavior above with focused regression coverage and documentation.\n\nValidation: deterministic regression tests and independent GitWeave review; GitHub CI on the published changes.\n\nCloses #50."
      }
